{"name":"Left Bank Blue","hex":"#699cab","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"left","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Designating the side of the body toward the west when one is facing north; the side of the body on which the heart is located in most humans; the opposite of right. This arrow points to the reader's left: ←","Anticlockwise, particularly when describing a change in direction or orientation."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["On the left side.","Towards the left side."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/left"},{"term":"bank","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An institution where one can place and borrow money and take care of financial affairs.","A branch office of such an institution."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To deal with a bank or financial institution, or for an institution to provide financial services to a client.","To put into a bank (financial institution)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bank"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bank (geography)","blocks":[{"text":"In geography, a bank is the land alongside a body of water. Different structures are referred to as \"banks\" in different fields of geography."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Perfume_River_Bank%2C_as_seen_from_Tr%C6%B0%E1%BB%9Dng_Ti%E1%BB%81n_Bridge%2C_2019.jpg/330px-Perfume_River_Bank%2C_as_seen_from_Tr%C6%B0%E1%BB%9Dng_Ti%E1%BB%81n_Bridge%2C_2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bank_(geography)","wikidata":"Q2897058"},{"title":"Bank","blocks":[{"text":"A bank is a financial institution that accepts deposits from the public and creates a demand deposit while making loans. Lending activities can be directly performed by the bank or indirectly through capital markets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/London.bankofengland.arp.jpg/330px-London.bankofengland.arp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bank","wikidata":"Q22687"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Kuekenhoff_Canal_002.jpg/500px-Kuekenhoff_Canal_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Kuekenhoff_Canal_002.jpg/500px-Kuekenhoff_Canal_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An artificial lake with grass banks in Keukenhof, Netherlands","link":"https://en.